From: openEuler RISC-V package contributors
Subject: [PATCH] configure: preserve incoming CFLAGS during compiler checks

Source: https://github.com/enferex/pdfresurrect/tree/7a57bffaa8e0ad47f9b0a4fa44fe5ae621680c62
Applies-to: Pdfresurrect 0.23, source archive SHA256 e47a75a328020e4ebac5768921daa50b77c30610e787f0e78139fd4766a970ed
License: configure.ac is covered by the project BSD-3-Clause grant. The checked-in configure retains its original FSF unlimited permission to copy, distribute and modify it; all original grants remain unchanged.
Upstream-Status: Not submitted; no upstream write performed.
Root-Cause: The hand-written CFLAGS clear around AC_PROG_CC drops the incoming compiler hardening flags while preserving hardened LDFLAGS. Exact target run 40613665527/a1 config.log shows an empty CFLAGS link at configure:2652 failing with R_RISCV_HI20 and fopen R_RISCV_CALL_PLT relocations; the missing conftest is a consequence, not a native execution diagnosis.
Scope: Remove only that clear in configure.ac and its checked-in generated counterpart; retain X save/restore, Autoconf's internal flag tests, the empty-input -O3 -Wall policy and all probes. Do not regenerate configure, skip a probe, change --host or weaken linker hardening.
Removal: Drop after a reviewed official stable source preserves incoming CFLAGS through these checks and passes the unchanged target build/install QA under the same hardening policy.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -12,4 +12,3 @@
-# Checks for programs, and clears CFLAGS during the check.
+# Checks for programs, preserving incoming CFLAGS during compiler checks.
 X="$CFLAGS"
-CFLAGS=""
 AC_PROG_CC
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -2157,4 +2157,3 @@
-# Checks for programs, and clears CFLAGS during the check.
+# Checks for programs, preserving incoming CFLAGS during compiler checks.
 X="$CFLAGS"
-CFLAGS=""
 ac_ext=c
